.TH BTK-PUBKEY 1 "15 August 2026" "Bitcoin Toolkit 4.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
btk-pubkey \- derive or recompress public keys
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B btk pubkey
[\fB\-\-compressed\fR | \fB\-\-uncompressed\fR]
[\fB\-\-from\fR \fIwif\fR|\fIhex\fR|\fIdec\fR]
[\fB\-\-source\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Derive a public key from an explicit private key, or parse and recompress a
public key. Items are read from stdin. There are no positional key arguments.
.PP
Each stdin item is a typed
.B privkey
or
.B pubkey
object, or a bare line determined in this order: WIF, 64-character hex
private key, a decimal digit string, then 66- or 130-character hex
public key.
.B \-\-from
overrides that determination.
.B \-\-from hex
accepts a 64-character private key or a 66- or 130-character public key.
.PP
Leftover text is an error. There is no
.B \-\-from text
or
.BR "\-\-from file" .
A WIF-shaped string with a bad checksum is
.BR "invalid WIF checksum" ,
not a public key.
.PP
Default compression follows the input (object field, WIF flag, or
.BR 02 / 03 / 04
prefix). Flags override. Both flags emit two objects. Output
.B encoding
is always hex.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show this help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-compressed
Emit a compressed public key (33 bytes,
.B 02
or
.B 03
prefix).
.TP
.B \-\-uncompressed
Emit an uncompressed public key (65 bytes,
.B 04
prefix). Both flags emit two objects (compressed first).
.TP
.BI \-\-from " wif|hex|dec"
Force how bare stdin lines are interpreted. Default is determined from
the input. Unknown
values are
.BR "invalid \-\-from" .
.TP
.B \-\-source
Include the input item as a
.B source
object. A typed object is copied as received, including a nested
.B source
if present. Omitted unless this flag is set. On a
bare string the source is synthesized (WIF/hex/dec private key or
hex public key); the
.B data
field is the bare input.
.TP
.BI \-\-network " mainnet|testnet"
Network for hex and decimal inputs. WIF version bytes and a typed object's
.B network
field take precedence. Default mainnet.
.TP
.BI \-\-out " ndjson|json|plain"
Output framing. Default ndjson.
.TP
.BI \-\-in " auto|ndjson|json|plain"
Stdin framing. Default auto.
.SH NOTES
.B source
is omitted unless
.B \-\-source
is given. Address must not walk
.B source
for network.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR btk (1),
.BR btk-privkey (1)
